Now I have enough to write my independent assessment. Let me synthesize my findings.

**Key findings from independent research:**
- Isaac Lab PR #3259 ("disjoint navigation") confirmed real and accurately characterized
- MoMaGen at ICLR 2026 confirmed (jiajunwu.com PDF verified)
- No April–May 2026 concurrent work found attacking the specific combination of coupled SE(3) stance encoding + stance-conditioned IRM for bipedal data generation + combinatorial composition
- "Stance-conditioned IRM for bipedal data generation" appears genuinely novel — no papers found applying IRM within a demo-multiplication retargeting loop for bipedals
- All cited papers (SoftMimicGen, ULTRA, DemoHLM, OmniRetarget, etc.) verified as real
- All three Round 8 required fixes are present in the submission

**Remaining structural concern:** The paper describes the τ sensitivity numbers ("35-40% yield reduction at 25th percentile, 5-8pp variance at 5th percentile") as "preliminary analysis estimates" while simultaneously claiming the 100-1,000× expansion range is "tied to this validated operating point." "Validated" contradicts "preliminary analysis" — one of these must give.

